---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import { FOUNDER, CONTACT_EMAIL, PILOT_HREF, INVESTOR_HREF, REPO_URL, VERSION, contactHref, contactLabel } from '../site';
---

<Base title="Company and product thesis" description="RigorRun is a founder-led, open-source agent verification project. The thesis: test permissions and scope from system evidence before deployment. Paid workflow pilots first; a team subscription is planned.">
  <Section>
    <div class="rr-prose-width">
      <Eyebrow>Company</Eyebrow>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-display font-medium text-balance">Agents need a release check for what they do, not just what they say.</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 text-lead text-secondary">RigorRun is building pre-deployment verification for tool-using AI agents. Start with permission and customer-scope failures, read the system afterwards, and keep the agent&rsquo;s claims separate from the evidence.</p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-support text-secondary">Founder-led by {FOUNDER}. The published MIT runner is <span class="font-mono">rigorrun@{VERSION}</span>. Current concrete examples are the multi-tenant Helpdesk twin and Stripe refunds; custom-system permission packs are not built yet.</p>
    </div>
  </Section>
  <Section ruled tight>
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.2fr] lg:gap-16">
      <div><h2 class="text-display font-medium text-balance">The investment thesis</h2></div>
      <div>
        <p class="text-lead text-secondary">When an agent gets tools and credentials, a plausible reply is no longer enough to check the work. Prompt, model and integration changes need regression tests for customer boundaries, allowed actions and actual side effects.</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-support text-secondary">The initial customer hypothesis is a CTO or AI/platform lead at a B2B SaaS team moving tool-using agents into customer workflows. The buying moment is a release, a security review or an incident that must not recur.</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-support text-muted">This is a product thesis, not a measured market-size or competitive-superiority claim. RigorRun complements runtime authorisation and monitoring; it does not replace them.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
  <Section ruled tight>
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.2fr] lg:gap-16">
      <div><h2 class="text-display font-medium text-balance">Open source for adoption. Workflow verification for revenue.</h2></div>
      <div>
        <p class="text-lead text-secondary">The runner stays MIT-licensed. The initial commercial offer is a paid, scoped pilot: make one real workflow testable, agree which defects it must catch, and hand off reproducible evidence and a release check.</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-support text-secondary">A shared team workspace is planned as the recurring product: workflow management, run history and approvals. It is not built yet. Willingness to pay, repeat usage and pricing remain validation questions.</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-support"><a class="rr-link" href="/access">Free runner, paid pilot and planned subscription</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
  <Section ruled tight>
    <h2 class="text-display font-medium text-balance">Next milestones, not traction claims</h2>
    <ol class="mt-8 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <li class="rounded-panel border border-line bg-surface p-6"><h3 class="text-title font-medium">Validate one real workflow</h3><p class="mt-3 text-support text-secondary">Find a design partner with a known failure, readable system state and a safe test environment. Custom integrations are scoped work, not assumed compatibility.</p></li>
      <li class="rounded-panel border border-line bg-surface p-6"><h3 class="text-title font-medium">Show repeated release use</h3><p class="mt-3 text-support text-secondary">Check whether the team reruns the suite after model, prompt and credential changes, and whether the evidence helps a real shipping decision.</p></li>
      <li class="rounded-panel border border-line bg-surface p-6"><h3 class="text-title font-medium">Validate the recurring product</h3><p class="mt-3 text-support text-secondary">Only then test demand for managed workflows, shared history and approvals. These are planned milestones, not current revenue or customer results.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-support text-muted">The technical starting point is public: <a class="rr-link" href="/replay/helpdesk">the recorded Helpdesk run</a>, <a class="rr-link" href="/replay">the Stripe recording</a> and <a class="rr-link" href="/evidence">the evidence with its limits</a>. Historical release evidence does not qualify an altered engine build.</p>
  </Section>
  <Section ruled tight>
    <div class="rr-prose-width">
      <h2 class="text-display font-medium text-balance">See the demo. Challenge the thesis.</h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lead text-secondary">For a hackathon, start with the recorded failure and its system evidence. For an engineering team or investor conversation, bring a workflow, a failure mode or a hard question.</p>
      <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><Button href={INVESTOR_HREF}>Discuss the thesis</Button><Button href={PILOT_HREF} variant="secondary">Discuss a paid pilot</Button><Button href={REPO_URL} variant="secondary" external>Source code</Button></div>
      <p class="mt-5 text-support"><a class="rr-link" href={contactHref(CONTACT_EMAIL)}>{contactLabel(CONTACT_EMAIL)}</a></p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
